---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Human-Directed Reactivity San Jacinto | Good Doggos";
const description = "Overcome human-directed reactivity in San Jacinto. We face the challenge of social stress with real control and stable leadership to take your social life back.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Human-Directed Reactivity Training",
  "description": description,
  "provider": {
    "@type": "LocalBusiness",
    "name": "Good Doggos",
    "url": "https://gooddoggos.com",
    "telephone": "+19514016252",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressLocality": "San Jacinto",
      "addressRegion": "CA",
      "addressCountry": "US"
    }
  },
  "areaServed": {
    "@type": "AdministrativeArea",
    "name": "Riverside County"
  },
  "url": "https://gooddoggos.com/services/human-directed-reactivity"
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Hero Band -->
  <section class="bg-primary-navy pt-32 pb-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-body text-white/50 mt-6 mb-4" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Home</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <a href="/services/aggression-rehabilitation" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Aggression Rehabilitation</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <span class="text-white/80 truncate">Human-Directed Reactivity</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-heading font-bold text-white leading-tight mb-6">
        Human-Directed Reactivity Training in San Jacinto
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Body Content -->
  <section class="py-16 px-4 bg-[#FCF9FA]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
      
      <!-- Main Content -->
      <div class="prose max-w-none">
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          If you’re crossing the street every time a neighbor walks toward you on State Street, you’re living in a state of hyper-vigilance. It’s socially isolating when you can’t have friends over to your San Jacinto home without worrying about a potential bite.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          These reactive outbursts are symptoms of social stress and a lack of leadership. Because we are professionals, we do not guess or give out generic advice. We must evaluate your dog in person to understand exactly what triggers their reactivity toward people. "Distracting with a cookie" doesn't work when a dog is already lunging; you need a real leadership plan.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-primary-navy mt-12 mb-6">
          Real Control for Social Stress
        </h2>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          At Good Doggos, I don't move around the danger of human-directed reactivity; I face it. For over 8 years, I’ve specialized in the dogs that make owners nervous—the ones that growl at the mailman or lunge at joggers in the Riverside County heat. My balanced approach is built on the reality that a reactive dog needs more than just a treat; they need a leader who can define what is off-limits.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          My confidence in these moments comes from my own origin story. After being bit as a child in Mexico, I had to master dog behavior strategies to overcome my fear. Because I’ve lived through the anxiety, I can provide the calm, stable "safe space" your dog needs. I don't see "bad" dogs; I see unguided dogs.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          I use high-value rewards to mark neutrality, but I also use calibrated leash corrections the moment a dog decides to fixate or escalate. If you don't interrupt the intent, you'll never change the outcome. Take the Camila case: she went from being labeled euthanize-ready by other trainers to walking peacefully with my helper dog Simba on her first day.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          We take the training to the real-world triggers of San Jacinto—practicing around the crowds at Valley-Wide Recreation or busy local neighborhoods. I’ll teach you how to be the advocate your dog needs while giving them the tools to exist in a human world safely. My goal is a dog that looks to you for direction the moment a stranger enters their space.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6 font-bold">
          Stop living in isolation. Apply for a Free Behavioral Assessment and take your social life back.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
     CTA BAND
══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[#FBF1E9]" style="border-top: 1px solid #E6DAC6;">
  <div class="w-full h-[3px]" style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #0F6D72, #D1B27F, #0F6D72);"></div>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-20 md:py-24 text-center">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-bold tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color: rgba(15,109,114,0.60);">Your Dog Is Next</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-4" style="color: #0B2744;">
      Ready to See What's Possible?<br/>
      <span class="headline-accent" style="color: #D1B27F; font-style: italic; font-weight: 700;">Start With a Free Assessment.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="text-base mb-10 max-w-lg mx-auto" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.60);">
      Tell us about your dog. We'll do an honest assessment and point you toward the right program — or tell you if we're not the right fit.
    </p>
    <a href="/apply"
       class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 font-bold text-sm tracking-widest uppercase rounded-full transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5"
       style="background: #D1B27F; color: #0B2744; padding: 18px 44px; box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(209,178,127,0.35);">
      Apply for Free Behavioral Assessment →
    </a>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.40);">Takes less than 3 minutes · No commitment required</p>
  </div>
</div>
</Layout>
